-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions of seat notified from part P0 (merged; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- P0-cases-seat-notified: the cases of the questions in P0-seat-notified.l4: the facts a person in the seat would state.
-- Every expected value was decided from the text of the Regulation before the file was run and is written beside its assertion with the words that license it;
-- none was copied from the encoding's output. A failing assertion is a finding, never an expectation to edit.
-- Dates the cases stand on: 31 July 2024 (the day before entry into force), 1 August 2024, 1 and 2 February 2025 (Chapter I), 26 and 27 July 2026 (each side of the Omnibus),
-- 1 and 2 August 2026 (the general date), 2 December 2026, 2 August 2027, 2 December 2027, 2 August 2028, 2 August 2030, 31 December 2030, as each function needs.
-- A MIRROR comment marks a case whose facts are asked, with the same answer, in the case file of another seat (the Guide, section 3).
-- A #TRACE is preceded by its -- EXPECT line (FULFILLED, BREACH or OPEN: the obligation still pending). The clock of a trace is the number of days since the day the rule counts from.
-- Assertions: 24. Traces: 0.

§ `Article 1: does Chapter I apply on the date asked?`

-- Under Article 1, as a notified body, does Chapter I apply on the date asked
-- 1 January 2024, before the Regulation exists: JUST FALSE, the Regulation has not entered into force (Art 113, first paragraph: "on the twentieth day following that of its publication")
#ASSERT `Under Article 1, as a notified body, does Chapter I apply on the date asked` (Date 1 1 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 31 July 2024, the day before entry into force: JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under Article 1, as a notified body, does Chapter I apply on the date asked` (Date 31 7 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 1 August 2024, in force but Chapter I applies only from 2 February 2025: JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under Article 1, as a notified body, does Chapter I apply on the date asked` (Date 1 8 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 1 February 2025, the day before Chapter I applies (Art 113(a)): JUST FALSE
-- MIRROR Art 113(a): whether Chapter I applies, asked from every seat
#ASSERT `Under Article 1, as a notified body, does Chapter I apply on the date asked` (Date 1 2 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 2 February 2025, the day Chapter I applies (Art 113(a)): JUST TRUE
-- MIRROR Art 113(a): whether Chapter I applies, asked from every seat
#ASSERT `Under Article 1, as a notified body, does Chapter I apply on the date asked` (Date 2 2 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 26 July 2026, the text as enacted still in force: JUST TRUE (as enacted point (a): "Chapters I and II shall apply from 2 February 2025")
#ASSERT `Under Article 1, as a notified body, does Chapter I apply on the date asked` (Date 26 7 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 27 July 2026, the text as amended: JUST TRUE (point (a) as replaced keeps 2 February 2025 for Chapters I and II)
#ASSERT `Under Article 1, as a notified body, does Chapter I apply on the date asked` (Date 27 7 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE


§ `Article 3(3) to (8): does the definition of my role fit me?`

-- Under Article 3(8), as a notified body, am I an operator
-- the seat's role is passed as the keel's `Role`: FALSE (the definition says "means" and the list ends with the distributor): the role of this seat is not an operator
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(8), as a notified body, am I an operator` EQUALS FALSE


§ `Article 3(21), (22): am I a notified body?`

-- Under Article 3(22), as a notified body, does the definition of a notified body fit me
-- a conformity assessment body notified under the Regulation and under other relevant legislation: TRUE
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(22), as a notified body, does the definition of a notified body fit me` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- does not perform third-party conformity assessment: FALSE (not a conformity assessment body)
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(22), as a notified body, does the definition of a notified body fit me` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- not notified under the Regulation: FALSE ("notified in accordance with this Regulation")
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(22), as a notified body, does the definition of a notified body fit me` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- not notified under other relevant Union harmonisation legislation that is relevant: FALSE ("and other relevant Union harmonisation legislation": fork F-3-22 of the keel)
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(22), as a notified body, does the definition of a notified body fit me` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE


§ `Article 3(23): substantial modification`

-- Under Article 3(23), as a notified body, is the change a substantial modification
-- after placing on the market, not foreseen, compliance affected: TRUE ("a change ... which is not foreseen or planned in the initial conformity assessment ... as a result of which the compliance ... is affected")
-- MIRROR Art 3(23): the same change asked from the provider, importer, distributor, deployer and notified body seats
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(23), as a notified body, is the change a substantial modification` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- after placing on the market, not foreseen, the intended purpose modified: TRUE ("or results in a modification to the intended purpose")
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(23), as a notified body, is the change a substantial modification` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- foreseen or planned in the initial conformity assessment: FALSE (the definition says "means")
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(23), as a notified body, is the change a substantial modification` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- made before the placing on the market: FALSE
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(23), as a notified body, is the change a substantial modification` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- neither compliance nor intended purpose affected: FALSE
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(23), as a notified body, is the change a substantial modification` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE


§ `Article 111 and Article 113: does the group General apply on the date asked?`

-- Under Article 111, as a notified body, does General apply on the date asked
-- 31 July 2024, before entry into force: JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under Article 111, as a notified body, does General apply on the date asked` (Date 31 7 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 2 February 2025, after Chapter I applies but before the general date: JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under Article 111, as a notified body, does General apply on the date asked` (Date 2 2 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 26 July 2026, the text as enacted: JUST FALSE (as enacted: "It shall apply from 2 August 2026")
-- MIRROR Art 113 second paragraph: whether the group General applies, asked from every seat
#ASSERT `Under Article 111, as a notified body, does General apply on the date asked` (Date 26 7 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 27 July 2026, the text as amended: JUST FALSE (the general date is still 2 August 2026)
#ASSERT `Under Article 111, as a notified body, does General apply on the date asked` (Date 27 7 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 1 August 2026, the day before the general date: JUST FALSE
-- MIRROR Art 113 second paragraph: whether the group General applies, asked from every seat
#ASSERT `Under Article 111, as a notified body, does General apply on the date asked` (Date 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 2 August 2026, the general date ("It shall apply from 2 August 2026"): JUST TRUE
-- MIRROR Art 113 second paragraph: whether the group General applies, asked from every seat
#ASSERT `Under Article 111, as a notified body, does General apply on the date asked` (Date 2 8 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 2 August 2030, long after: JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under Article 111, as a notified body, does General apply on the date asked` (Date 2 8 2030) EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions of seat notified from part P2 (merged; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- P2-cases-seat-notified.l4: cases for every question of P2-seat-notified.l4, with the facts a real a notified body would state. Expected values are written by hand from the text.

§ `The role and the applicability of the provisions`

-- a conformity assessment body notified under this Regulation and any other relevant legislation
#ASSERT `Under Article 11, as a notified body, am I a notified body within the meaning of Article 3(22)` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not notified under the other relevant legislation that applies
#ASSERT `Under Article 11, as a notified body, am I a notified body within the meaning of Article 3(22)` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not notified under this Regulation
#ASSERT `Under Article 11, as a notified body, am I a notified body within the meaning of Article 3(22)` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- the day before Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply to an Annex III system (Art 113(c)(i)): they do not apply
#ASSERT `Under Article 8, as a notified body, does Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply on the date asked` (Date 1 12 2027) `Route Article 6(2) and Annex III` (Date 2 12 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the day they begin to apply to an Annex III system
#ASSERT `Under Article 8, as a notified body, does Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply on the date asked` (Date 2 12 2027) `Route Article 6(2) and Annex III` (Date 2 12 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an Annex I system on 2 December 2027: its date is 2 August 2028 (Art 113(c)(ii))
#ASSERT `Under Article 8, as a notified body, does Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply on the date asked` (Date 2 12 2027) `Route Article 6(1) and Annex I` (Date 2 12 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the day before they apply to an Annex I system
#ASSERT `Under Article 8, as a notified body, does Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply on the date asked` (Date 1 8 2028) `Route Article 6(1) and Annex I` (Date 1 8 2028) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the day they begin to apply to an Annex I system
#ASSERT `Under Article 8, as a notified body, does Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply on the date asked` (Date 2 8 2028) `Route Article 6(1) and Annex I` (Date 2 8 2028) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- placed earlier and not significantly changed: saved by Article 111(2)
#ASSERT `Under Article 8, as a notified body, does Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply on the date asked` (Date 2 12 2030) `Route Article 6(2) and Annex III` (Date 1 1 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- placed earlier and significantly changed since: covered
#ASSERT `Under Article 8, as a notified body, does Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply on the date asked` (Date 2 12 2030) `Route Article 6(2) and Annex III` (Date 1 1 2027) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a system that is not high-risk: no date of application, they do not apply
#ASSERT `Under Article 8, as a notified body, does Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply on the date asked` (Date 2 12 2030) `Route neither` (Date 2 12 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE


§ `Under Annex IV: the technical documentation`

-- MIRROR Art IV-1: the same facts are asked from the seat of a provider of an AI system (P2-cases-seat-provider.l4); the answers agree
-- every element of the text is met
#ASSERT `Under Annex IV point 1, as a notified body, does the technical documentation I was given contain a general description of the AI system including the eight items the point lists` (Date 2 12 2027) `Route Article 6(2) and Annex III` (Date 2 12 2027) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not met: the technical documentation contains a general description of the AI system
#ASSERT `Under Annex IV point 1, as a notified body, does the technical documentation I was given contain a general description of the AI system including the eight items the point lists` (Date 2 12 2027) `Route Article 6(2) and Annex III` (Date 2 12 2027) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not met: the technical documentation contains its intended purpose, the name of the provider and the version of the system reflecting its relation to previous versions
